     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.75, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.9, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid triage that correctly identifies the attack vector and justifies the medium severity appropriately. The severity reasoning is particularly strong\u2014the analyst clearly articulates why a blocked attack with no internal impact warrants medium rather than high or critical severity. The ATT&CK citations are reasonable (T1190 is the primary fit for public-facing application exploitation), though T1210 and T1068 are somewhat tangential since the attack was blocked and there was no actual privilege escalation or remote service exploitation. Consider narrowing to the most directly applicable technique. The investigation could be slightly more complete by explicitly noting whether the F5 ASM blocking action was verified in the alert itself, and by suggesting a check of recent ASM rule updates to confirm current coverage. The recommended response is thorough and actionable. Overall, this meets triage-quality standards.\"}",
     "type": "text"
    }
